From 604de859a6a16aea666d98edd74c1c115de30ec1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BearddOddity <beardedoddity@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 08:18:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Mod API: client-side modules written against one small,
 stable interface

A module is a folder in the player's Mods folder: a module.json that names it, the interface it was written for and every
event it listens to, and a module.js whose default export is setup(dfo). The interface is append-only, so a module written
for api 1 runs on every later game, and a module is updated by its author without a game release.

- src/mods/modApi.js: the manifest law, the version law, the event table (questMark, quests, mapPick, drawFx) and the bus;
  each module's handle: on, store, say, t (words in the player's language, from the game's own table), onKey, retarget,
  markColour. A failing module is isolated and switched off; one the player switched off is never imported.
- src/mods/moduleHost.js, modBus.js, keysPanel.js (Shift+F1: the player's keys for every module action), src/ui/modulesCard.js
  (Settings > Mods & files > Modules), app/lib/moduleFiles.cjs (the Mods folder, read by plain slug and file name only).
- The seams: ui/enhancedHud.js (questMark; the compass follows a module's retarget and colour), scenes/hostMagic.js (drawFx,
  with a read-only world probe: floor, ray, doors, known, waypoints), scenes/questBridge.js (quests), ui/heldMap.js,
  townSheet.js, automapSheet.js (mapPick).
- Quest guidance that follows the journal: an entry that says where a person waits points at their building or town
  (questLens personSiteOf); a person the quest is done with is marked no more (questGuidance personDealtWith); a town the
  entry names but the map lacks is ringed on the region map (seek).
- Client-side only: nothing reaches the net; no wire or relay change.

The first modules, Beardd's Wayfarer (a quest waypoint, pins, a guide trail), live in their own repository:
github.com/BearddOddity/beardds-wayfarer. Specification: bible/06-Systems/Mod-API.md. Tests: test/mods1_api.test.js and the
quest guidance tests (guide1, guide5, guide8).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
